<title>HUNGARY: PICK PLANS 20PCT '96 DIVIDEND VS 15PCT '95.</title>
<headline>PICK PLANS 20PCT '96 DIVIDEND VS 15PCT '95.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian meat processor Pick Szeged Rt said on Wednesday its management would propose a payout of a 20 percent dividend, or 200 forints per share, on the 1996 results.</p>
<p>The company paid a 15 percent dividend last year.</p>
<p>Pick, which posted a consolidated pre-tax profit of 2.48 billion forints on net sales of 28.56 billion in 1996, will hold its annual shareholders meeting on April 28, the company said in an announcement published in the official bourse gazette.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
